<page xmlns="http://projectmallard.org/1.0/" type="topic" id="canvas-editing">
  <info><link type="guide" xref="canvas"/><desc>Draw, Erase, and Crop in coyote.</desc></info>
  <title>Draw, Erase, and Crop</title>
  <p>Choose <gui>File</gui> → <gui>New</gui> for a blank drawing, <gui>Import...</gui> for PNG, JPEG, or static SVG, or <gui>Edit</gui> → <gui>Paste</gui> for a PNG or JPEG offered by the clipboard. Select the <gui>Pencil</gui>, <gui>Eraser</gui>, or <gui>Crop</gui> icon below the menu bar, or use the matching <gui>Edit</gui> menu item. The active icon is highlighted. Hover over an icon to see its name. <gui>Pencil</gui> is selected by default.</p>
  <p>Draw with the pen tip or mouse. Select <gui>Eraser</gui> in the toolbar or <gui>Edit</gui> menu to remove ink with a 16-pixel brush without changing the background. A tablet tool recognized as an eraser temporarily erases for that gesture without changing the selected tool; selected <gui>Crop</gui> takes precedence. Release to apply the stroke; <gui>Undo</gui> and <gui>Redo</gui> act on the whole gesture. Press <key>Escape</key> to cancel a gesture in progress.</p>
  <p>Select <gui>Crop</gui> in the toolbar or <gui>Edit</gui> menu, then drag the rectangle with the pen or mouse or enter exact pixel bounds. The toolbar and menu remain available to leave a pending crop when the working copy is editable; both are disabled when no editable working copy is available or <gui>Show Markup</gui> is off. Switching to <gui>Pencil</gui> or <gui>Eraser</gui> discards the pending crop. Only <gui>Apply Crop</gui> commits it. <gui>Apply Crop</gui>, <gui>Cancel</gui>, and <key>Escape</key> return to the drawing tool selected before <gui>Crop</gui>. Crop does not resample pixels, and zoom changes only the view. No new shortcuts are assigned; Tab and arrow keys use native toolbar navigation, and Edit menu mnemonics remain available.</p>
  <p>Choose <guiseq><gui>View</gui><gui>Fit</gui></guiseq> to show the full drawing in the current viewport, or <guiseq><gui>View</gui><gui>Actual Size</gui></guiseq> for 100%. Fit works on the working copy and saved revisions, and it preserves any pending crop. It changes only the display scale, not the drawing or its attachments.</p>
</page>
